  "content": {
    "id": "p5-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "State the global minimum and maximum of these functions. A sketch can help.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=x^2,\\quad -2\\le x\\le2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $0$. Global maximum: $4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=2x\\\\2x&=0\\\\x&=0\\end{aligned}$$\nCompare $f(-2)=4$, $f(0)=0$ and $f(2)=4$.\nGlobal minimum: $0$ at $x=0$. Global maximum: $4$ at $x=\\pm2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=5-x,\\quad 0\\le x\\le3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $2$. Global maximum: $5$.",
          "worked": "$f'(x)=-1$, so the function decreases throughout the domain.\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(0)&=5\\\\f(3)&=2\\end{aligned}$$\nGlobal minimum: $2$ at $x=3$. Global maximum: $5$ at $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=\\sqrt{16-x^2},\\quad -4\\le x\\le4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $0$. Global maximum: $4$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{-x}{\\sqrt{16-x^2}}\\\\f'(x)&=0\\quad\\text{at }x=0\\end{aligned}$$\nCompare $f(-4)=0$, $f(0)=4$ and $f(4)=0$.\nGlobal minimum: $0$ at $x=\\pm4$. Global maximum: $4$ at $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-q2-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$y=|x|,\\quad -5\\le x\\le1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $0$. Global maximum: $5$.",
          "worked": "The derivative is undefined at $x=0$, the vertex of the graph.\nCompare $f(-5)=5$, $f(0)=0$ and $f(1)=1$.\nGlobal minimum: $0$ at $x=0$. Global maximum: $5$ at $x=-5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$y=\\sqrt{x},\\quad 0\\le x\\le8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $0$. Global maximum: $2\\sqrt2$.",
          "worked": "For $x>0$, $f'(x)=\\frac1{2\\sqrt{x}}>0$, so the function increases.\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(0)&=0\\\\f(8)&=\\sqrt8=2\\sqrt2\\end{aligned}$$\nGlobal minimum: $0$ at $x=0$. Global maximum: $2\\sqrt2$ at $x=8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac1x,\\quad -4\\le x\\le-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $-1$. Global maximum: $-\\frac14$.",
          "worked": "$f'(x)=-\\frac1{x^2}<0$ throughout the domain, so the function decreases.\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(-4)&=-\\frac14\\\\f(-1)&=-1\\end{aligned}$$\nGlobal minimum: $-1$ at $x=-1$. Global maximum: $-\\frac14$ at $x=-4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$y=3x^2-16x+5,\\quad 0\\le x\\le4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $-\\frac{49}{3}$. Global maximum: $5$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=6x-16\\\\6x-16&=0\\\\x&=\\frac83\\\\f(0)&=5\\\\f\\left(\\frac83\\right)&=3\\left(\\frac83\\right)^2-16\\left(\\frac83\\right)+5\\\\f\\left(\\frac83\\right)&=-\\frac{49}{3}\\\\f(4)&=-11\\end{aligned}$$\nGlobal minimum: $-\\frac{49}{3}$ at $x=\\frac83$. Global maximum: $5$ at $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$y=\\sqrt[3]{x^2},\\quad -2\\le x\\le8$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $0$. Global maximum: $4$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, $f'(x)=\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{x}}$, which is never zero. The derivative is undefined at $x=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(-2)&=\\sqrt[3]4\\\\f(0)&=0\\\\f(8)&=4\\end{aligned}$$\nGlobal minimum: $0$ at $x=0$. Global maximum: $4$ at $x=8$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$y=-3x^4-4x^3+12x^2+3,\\quad x\\in[-2,2]$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Global minimum: $-29$. Global maximum: $35$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=-12x^3-12x^2+24x\\\\f'(x)&=-12x(x+2)(x-1)\\\\-12x(x+2)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=-2,\\ 0,\\ 1\\\\f(-2)&=35\\\\f(0)&=3\\\\f(1)&=8\\\\f(2)&=-29\\end{aligned}$$\nGlobal minimum: $-29$ at $x=2$. Global maximum: $35$ at $x=-2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$y=\\frac1{x-2},\\quad -3\\le x\\le3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "No global minimum or global maximum; the function is unbounded below and above.",
          "worked": "The function is undefined at $x=2$, so its domain is $[-3,2)\\cup(2,3]$.\nAs $x$ approaches $2$ from below, $f(x)$ decreases without bound. As $x$ approaches $2$ from above, $f(x)$ increases without bound.\nTherefore there is no global minimum and no global maximum. Infinity is not an attained function value.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 31
      }
    ]
